                        "glosses": [
                            "made of cotton in imitation of parchment."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "of paper"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "32f0ecc2-4b41-4463-994e-388ed361009f",
                                "sense_id": "deb06be8-9381-3165-bfd1-6ff80cabe202",
                                "text": "The necessity of finding a substitute for parchment , which was very costly, led to the inventio , in imitation of the bombycinous paper — such was the name given to the cotton paper of the East - of paper made of rags, some say at Basle in 1170, by Greek refugees; others say at Padua in 1301, by an Italian named Pax."
                            },
